  "_README": "Exchange trading-calendar exceptions, keyed by the exchange codes in lib/sessions.js (SEHK/KRX/TWSE/TSE/EURONEXT/XETRA/LSE/US/UAE). Per exchange: 'closed' = full-day closures, 'half' = early-close (half) sessions. Years not yet in the file are generated by scripts/holidays-fetch.py (exchange_calendars, recorded under _generated); a year already present is never touched, so hand corrections stand. Dates are the exchange's LOCAL calendar date (YYYY-MM-DD). marketState() returns 'holiday' on a 'closed' date; the Pre-Read adds a 'HALF DAY' heads-up when a region's exchange is on a 'half' date. SAFE-DEGRADING: a MISSING date just falls back to normal behavior; only a WRONG date mislabels a real session, so verify before adding. The exact early-close TIME is not modeled (the Pre-Read fires pre-open, so it only needs the heads-up). Seeded 2026-07-15 for the remainder of 2026, verified against exchange/aggregator calendars; lunar-based dates (Chuseok, Mid-Autumn) especially warrant a re-check each year. UAE (DFM/ADX) is kept by scripts/holidays-uae.mjs from DFM's own circulars (lib/uaeHolidays.js): moon holidays sit in UAE.tentative until DFM's circular confirms them, and only then move to UAE.closed; _uae records the check, the source of each date and which dates the script wrote (anything else in UAE.closed was entered by hand and stands).",
